    "guidance": "Validated in distribution on the 12 replayed training-segment entry states: 10/12 final successes (83.3%). Invoke only in the documented regime: drawer_position > 0.26 m, red being released or settled on its outside pad, blue observed outside as the source, with source_object=\"blue\" and destination_field=\"blue_goal\". Its source-frame representation is intended for pickup and early carry when source displacement/rotation is the main concern, but that benefit has not been validated out of distribution. Avoid using it as the preferred confined final-alignment policy, for unreachable/collision-prone source poses, or as recovery after a suspected drop or impact. Monitor IK convergence/limit contacts, whether blue and TCP co-move after closure, red remaining on the pad, and approach to the drawer lip/wall. In both validation failures the drawer stayed open and red stayed on-pad, but blue was not inside; those runs had 73 and 65 IK-unconverged steps. IK warnings are not conclusive, however, because one successful run had 335. Replan after each eight-action chunk. Once blue appears stably carried near the drawer, hand off to destination-anchored h02; on simultaneous drawer-open/red-on-pad/blue-inside success, hand only to framework evaluation. There is no learned successor or demonstrated recovery behavior."
